{
  "objects": "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product normed space with its Borel measurable structure; gamma_E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability. H_j is the unnormalized probabilists Hermite polynomial, with Gaussian squared norm j!. L2 means the actual real square-integrable equivalence-class Hilbert space.",
  "interface": {
    "id": "F1",
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.standard_gaussian_polynomial_ridge_L2_smooth",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product normed space E with its Borel structure and every real polynomial p, each literal ridge x -> p(<w,x>) belongs to L2(gamma_E). There exists a family h(w) of those membership proofs such that w -> (h(w)).toLp of that literal function is globally C-infinity on all of E into L2(gamma_E). No unit-vector, degree, coefficient or derivative bound is assumed."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "Definitions receive no theorem credit.",
    "No infinite-Hermite convergence or derivative limit is proved here.",
    "No identification of different feature Hilbert carriers is asserted.",
    "No ambient Gram formula away from unit directions follows from the unit-direction Gram identity."
  ]
}
